caption: Strength and Support — Overview
technology-rule: overview

Every strong part needs enough structure, power, cooling, and control behind it.

Arm ST, Striking ST, Lifting ST, full ST, and chassis ST are separate. A strong limb does not automatically strengthen the entire body. Support caps are permissions, not free points.

| Trait | Base Cost | What It Improves | Minimum Support |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Arm ST | 3/level for one arm; 5/level for both | Strength of arms for striking, gripping, grappling, and arm tasks | Local anchoring and reinforced joints |
| Striking ST | 5/level | Thrust and swing damage from body attacks | Reinforced striking limbs, joints, and shock absorption |
| Lifting ST | 3/level | Basic Lift, carrying, bracing, dragging, and whole-body labor | Spine, hips, bracing legs, and frame |
| Full ST | 10/level | All normal ST functions and HP unless separated | Full anatomical cyberframe |
| Chassis ST | Template value | Machine-body or vehicle-scale strength | Class III body template |

| Support Element | What It Does | Common Traits It Enables |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Frame / skeleton | Carries force and prevents self-injury. | Arm ST, Lifting ST, full ST, HP, heavy DR |
| Power source | Runs actuators, processors, sensors, armor, weapons, and life support. | Energy Reserve, high ST, active defenses, weapons |
| Heat management | Sheds waste heat from movement, processors, and weapons. | Sustained output, reduced recharge, sealed systems |
| Neural control | Lets the user control the hardware safely. | Combat Reflexes, Enhanced Tracking, CM, complex locomotion |
| Maintenance access | Allows service without dismantling the body. | Reduced downtime, field repair, reliable operation |
| Software security | Protects networked systems. | Cyberdecks, drone control, remote diagnostics |
| Legal/social tolerance | Determines whether the body can operate openly. | Licenses, permits, social access, public use |

ONE ARM IS NOT A FORKLIFT

Add spine, hip, and leg support before buying significant Lifting ST or full ST.
